source_expression:
\begin{definition}
\label{definition-opposite}
Given a $k$-algebra $A$ we denote $A^{op}$ the $k$-algebra we get by
reversing the order of multiplication in $A$. This is called the
{\it opposite algebra}.
\end{definition}

