source_expression:
\begin{definition}
\label{definition-brauer-group}
Let $k$ be a field. The {\it Brauer group} of $k$ is the abelian group
of similarity classes of finite central simple $k$-algebras defined
above. Notation $\text{Br}(k)$.
\end{definition}

